M5Stamp ESP32-P4 + C6 SDIO Linux  (NOMMU, BusyBox)

Account m5.  The password is password= in credentials.txt on the USB drive
(root: /tmp/credentials.txt).  Edit it and save: the board writes the drive
to flash a few seconds later and applies it.  No eject or reboot is needed.
su asks for root_password= from credentials.txt; SSH as root needs a
root_authorized_keys file on the drive.

Commands
  files    ls cp mv rm mkdir find xargs stat tree du df tar gzip unzip
  text     cat less head tail grep sed awk cut sort uniq wc tr diff vi
  system   ps top free uptime dmesg kill pkill pgrep watch timeout lsmod
  network  ifconfig ip ping nslookup traceroute netstat nc wget arp
  users    id whoami who w last su passwd
  other    python3 (MicroPython)  hexdump xxd md5sum sha256sum date bc

Autorun: main.py, main.sh or main on the USB drive runs as m5 at boot and
again when you save a new version.  easystick-autorun status|log|stop|start

Full list: busybox --list ; busybox-tools --list
Not available: sudo, nano, curl, file (no MMU on this CPU).
